WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.860
A legendary warrior-queen, 10,000&nbsp;
ships, and one heck of a shattered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:08.820
glass ceiling — but what does any of&nbsp;
this have to do with House of the Dragon?

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:13.560
In "The Black Queen," the first season&nbsp;
finale of HBO's massively successful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:18.540
Game of Thrones prequel House of the Dragon,&nbsp;
the Targaryen civil war known as the Dance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.220
of the Dragons begins in earnest. In the&nbsp;
Green corner, you've got Alicent Hightower,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:28.320
the widow of King Viserys Targaryen and&nbsp;
mother to Aegon Targaryen, the young king&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.760
she just installed on the Iron Throne. As&nbsp;
for the Blacks, there's Rhaenyra Targaryen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.140
daughter to Viserys and his intended heir,&nbsp;
who has spent her whole life preparing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.460
sit on the throne. Once childhood friends and&nbsp;
confidantes, these two women have spent their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:46.080
adult years completely at odds, especially as&nbsp;
their children have fought amongst each other.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.920
During the events of "The Black Queen,"&nbsp;
Alicent's father and Hand of the King&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.580
Otto Hightower tries to bargain with&nbsp;
Rhaenyra on his daughter's behalf,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.620
and in doing so, he brings her a small token&nbsp;
of the former friendship between the two women.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.520
When Otto approaches Rhaenyra and&nbsp;
her formidable husband Daemon on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.760
the bridge that leads to Dragonstone,&nbsp;
he tries to make a bargain with them:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:10.800
if they bend the knee to Aegon and accept him&nbsp;
as their king, he'll let Rhaenyra and her sons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.600
keep Dragonstone. He also suggests that her&nbsp;
sons will serve as squires and cupbearers to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.100
Alicent's children. Daemon definitely doesn't&nbsp;
mince words about his feelings on the matter.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:24.720
Understandably, Rhaenyra feels the&nbsp;
same way, going so far as to throw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:29.820
Otto's pin, signifying his status as Hand,&nbsp;
into the sea. This betrayal of Rhaenyra's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:34.140
father's wishes clearly infuriates both&nbsp;
her and Daemon, but at the last minute,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.480
Otto produces a gift from Alicent meant for&nbsp;
Rhaenyra that seems to soften her just a little.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.980
Otto gives Rhaenyra an envelope containing&nbsp;
a torn page from a book that she and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:47.820
Alicent read together when they were&nbsp;
young. That page focuses on Nymeria,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:52.740
a fierce warrior who brought a fleet of&nbsp;
10,000 ships across the Narrow Sea when she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:57.240
faced attacks from enemies in Valyria. When the&nbsp;
two girls read it in the show's first episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:02.007
they're still close friends, and clearly the&nbsp;
page brings back some memories for Rhaenyra.

00:02:04.046 --> 00:02:05.612
"What are you doing?"
"So you remember."

00:02:05.612 --> 00:02:10.800
Alicent seems to be missing a huge part of the&nbsp;
story, however, in that Nymeria ended up taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.660
over the region of Dorne and ruling as queen.&nbsp;
After her husband Mors Martell died in battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:19.800
Nymeria became a warrior in her own&nbsp;
right, and vanquished enough of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:23.880
opponents to fully rule Dorne and end&nbsp;
the tradition of male primogeniture.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:28.140
As both Rhaenys and Rhaenyra have directly&nbsp;
told Alicent during House of the Dragon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:32.340
the widowed queen has proven herself to be&nbsp;
perfectly happy to follow the lead of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:36.727
men in her life time and time again,&nbsp;
rarely striking out on her own terms.

00:02:36.727 --> 00:02:41.176
"You desire not to be free, but to make&nbsp;
a window in the wall of your prison." 

00:02:41.176 --> 00:02:46.020
Beyond that, Nymeria would certainly have harsh&nbsp;
words for a woman who is actively supplanting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:51.060
another woman's legitimate claim to the throne&nbsp;
by insisting that only a man can rule. Clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:55.500
Rhaenyra internalized a lot more about&nbsp;
Nymeria than Alicent did — then again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.500 --> 00:03:00.360
after the end of the episode, it's clear that&nbsp;
Alicent's gesture won't even matter going forward.

